-- title:
--   Lemma 3.16: Central cone induces a pointed l-cone
-- statement:
--   All vector spaces and Lie algebras are finite dimensional and real, with their usual Hausdorff topology. An invariant set is invariant under the group generated by $e^{\operatorname{ad}y}$. A closed convex set is pointed when its recession edge is zero. Write $\mathcal O_x=\operatorname{Inn}(\mathfrak g)x$, $\operatorname{co}(x)=\overline{\operatorname{conv}}\mathcal O_x$, and $C_x=\operatorname{cone}(\mathcal O_x)$. Admissibility means existence of a pointed generating invariant closed convex subset.
--
--   Let $\mathfrak g$ be admissible in its structural presentation and suppose $\mathfrak l$ acts faithfully on $V$. For any pointed closed convex cone $C_z\subseteq\mathfrak z$, put
--
--   $$W_l(C_z)=\{y\in\mathfrak l:\forall v\in V,\ [v,[v,y]]\in C_z\}.$$
--
--   Then $W_l(C_z)$ is a pointed invariant closed convex cone in $\mathfrak l$. No generation is claimed. Faithfulness is the subsection standing assumption.
-- source:
--   Elements in pointed invariant cones in Lie algebras and corresponding affine pairs, arXiv:2110.07297v1, PDF p. 13, Lemma 3.16: Central cone induces a pointed l-cone

